  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 6.2: \"Probability of Finding Correct Cascade without Supplement\", for 10, 100 and 1000 agents. All three curves lie on top of one another within their error bars — about 0.50 at signal strength 0.5, 0.67 at 0.6, 0.80 at 0.7, 0.93 at 0.8, and 1.0 by 0.9 — so the figure's content is a NEGATIVE: without the supplement, population size makes no visible difference to the chance of a correct cascade. Read against Figure 6.1, that is what isolates the subsidy as the cause there.",
